{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Fear not, worm.</b> For Israel was accounted as a worm in the eyes of the Babylonians, and the meaning is: fear not lest you be killed along with the Babylonians." "<b>For I am your help.</b> Past tense in place of future, and the meaning is that all future decrees are accounted as though they already are, and furthermore because past and future apply to created beings alone."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:23.169503700Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}